    "updated_at": "2015-10-26T10:32:02Z",
    "body": "To me they are two different issues (and gecko doesn't properly handle seek with readyState = HAVE_NOTHING). Throwing an exception when no resource is attached appears like the right thing to do.\n\nIn any case, you also need to modify in 4.8.13.7 , the definition of HAVE_METADATA which currently contains:\n\"The API will no longer throw an exception when seeking.\"\n",
